            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "src/report_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Michal Orzel",
                        "email": "michalx.orzel@intel.com",
                        "username": "morzelx"
                    },
                    "message": "Will You investigate that or is it up to Patrick to handle?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/report_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Reflecting on it more, i am not sure if it is design intent that PDI headers do not include each other.\n\n### Alternative 1 (i prefer this one)\n\n- PDI headers do not include each other\n- including one header might cause compilation failure if a dependent header is not also included\n- all interfaces which are used must be included => code remains searchable\n\n### Alternative 2\n\n- This is a bug and the `ReportManager/common.hpp` must include the header it depends on\n- An interface can be used without explicitly including it -> code is less searchable\n\n@patrick@stwcx.xyz what are your thoughts on it?\n\nFor now i removed these comments again since the PDI change for the namespace paths has been merged and we can include the `Telemetry.Report` header for the namespace path."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/report_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I thought there was code in the generator to add includes for enums from one interface to another that are used.  I'm surprised this didn't work but I'm not sure off-hand why it is broken.\n\nAs far as the search-ability, I think that clang-tidy IWYU can take care of this.  If someone really is using the other header, then it should be included, but if it is just a transitive use then it wouldn't be included."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/report_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Agree. It's not an issue in this patch anymore (since both headers are used), marking as resolved."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/report_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "new change to include the headers that `common.hpp` depends on:\n\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/sdbusplus/+/87327"
                }
            ],
